signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Milestone: plan review PASS/certified and ticket claimed. Created fresh worktree /Users/joeoakhart/fix9-mudbrick from origin/main for isolated implementation. Beginning RED-first tests for distinct gate_ref_hash_basis diagnostics.","timestamp":1788796876317460001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Milestone: RED-first tests added in tests/unit/test_gate_ref_hash_basis.py. RED evidence: initial run failed because both unresolvable-ref and materialization-failure arms logged the same generic 'current gate-ref snapshot unavailable' message. Implementation split resolve_ref and cache.acquire handling; targeted tests plus tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_ref_coherence.py now pass (11 passed). Sandboxed mutation removing the resolved-SHA materialization wording made the held-out materialization test fail, then implementation was restored.","timestamp":1788797114464939001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Milestone: full local verification passed with the required environment-clean make verify command; committed be11c06536ba with rebar-ticket trailer and DCO; verify-commit-ticket OK. Pushed to Gerrit as change 2793: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2793. Waiting for LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","timestamp":1788799616612126001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Milestone: Gerrit change 2793 submitted and origin/main now contains rebased merged commit a3a1fc5d508a70ecdd911e004c7b4dc1c8fbcb17. Local review commit be11c06536ba is superseded by Gerrit's rebased merge result; closing with --ref a3a1fc5d508a70ecdd911e004c7b4dc1c8fbcb17 to verify the landed tree.","timestamp":1788801570883567001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787964747709426785,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"029e1062-e852-4f61-b159-6a7657d2cc85","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"505d-b2c5-734f-47d9"},{"link_uuid":"170eab15-2431-4737-8171-6ee0d16919fa","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1edf-2504-2577-4b32"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n**This is a DIAGNOSABILITY fix, not a correctness one. The behaviour is already safe.**\nRead this first so nobody later mistakes it for another fail-open: bug\n`505d-b2c5-734f-47d9` made the claim gate fail CLOSED on a degraded basis, so whichever\nway the resolution fails the gate now refuses to certify. Nothing here changes a verdict.\nWhat is left is that an operator reading the box's logs cannot tell WHICH failure happened.\n\n`gate_ref_hash_basis()` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py`, added by 505d) wraps the\nwhole resolution in one broad `except Exception` and emits a single message:\n\n    current gate-ref snapshot unavailable; hashing the working tree\n\nTwo materially different faults collapse into that one line:\n\n1. **The ref does not resolve** — `resolve_ref(...)` raises `SnapshotRefError`. Benign and\n   expected in an ephemeral clone: the review-bot's `clone_change_ref` does `git init` +\n   `git fetch <url> <patchset-ref>` and configures no `origin` remote at all, so this fires\n   on 100% of review-bot runs. It is NOT actionable.\n2. **The ref resolved but the snapshot could not be materialized** — `_cache.acquire(...)`\n   raises. On the box's blobless checkout this is the interesting case:\n   `repo_snapshot._ensure_blobs_present` is documented \"Deliberately BEST-EFFORT and silent\n   on failure\", so a failed blob top-up plus a failed lazy fetch surfaces here. Disk\n   pressure, a corrupt or evicted cache entry, and a lock timeout land here too. This IS\n   actionable.\n\nCase 1 is routine noise; case 2 means the box cannot read the tree its gates are supposed\nto verify against. Today they are indistinguishable without attaching a debugger, so triage\nhas to guess — and because case 1 is so loud, case 2 is easy to dismiss as more of the same.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nThe log distinguishes the two, and the distinction is available to a caller that wants to\nreport it. An unresolvable ref stays a low-noise, expected outcome; a materialization\nfailure is identifiable as a distinct, operator-actionable fault.\n\n## Approach\n\nKeep it small. Inside `gate_ref_hash_basis` only:\n\n1. Split the single `try` so `resolve_ref` and `_cache.acquire` are caught separately, and\n   emit a distinct message for each (naming the ref in both cases; naming the resolved SHA\n   in the materialization case).\n2. Narrow the catches to what those calls actually raise (`SnapshotRefError` /\n   `SnapshotFetchError` for the ref arm), keeping a broad backstop so the function retains\n   its never-raises contract — that contract is load-bearing and must not regress.\n3. Optionally record which of the two occurred on `GateRefBasis` (e.g. a `cause` field), so\n   the claim gate's denial reason can say \"could not be resolved\" vs \"could not be\n   materialized\". Only if it stays cheap; the log split is the required part.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Any change to WHETHER the basis degrades, or to the fail-closed guard 505d added.\n- Any change to `_hash_basis`'s signature, contract, or working-tree fallback (ADR 0002; the\n  operator-approved decision on `72d9-8fbd-3a9e-48a6`).\n- Fixing the underlying materialization failures themselves.\n- Any new verdict literal. `bugfix_size_gate.KNOWN_VERDICTS` stays untouched.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] An unresolvable gate ref and a failed snapshot materialization emit DISTINCT log\n      messages, each naming the ref (and the materialization case naming the resolved SHA).\n- [x] `gate_ref_hash_basis` still never raises, and still returns the working-tree path with\n      `degraded=True` for BOTH faults — the 505d fail-closed behaviour is unchanged.\n- [x] `source=local` is still not reported as degraded.\n- [x] A test drives both arms separately and asserts the two are distinguishable (the\n      materialization arm by making `_cache.acquire` fail with the ref resolvable, so it is\n      not merely the ref arm again).\n- [x] `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_ref_coherence.py` stays green unchanged, including\n      `test_attested_claim_gate_refuses_to_certify_when_the_gate_ref_is_unresolvable`.\n- [x] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the default pytest suite exit zero.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py","reason":"split gate-ref resolution and materialization diagnostics"},{"path":"tests/unit/llm/plan_review/test_manifest.py","reason":"tests for distinct degraded-basis failure modes"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_ref_coherence.py","reason":"existing regression suite required to stay green unchanged"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","1edf-2504-2577-4b32"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"98ce43e1-172c-403f-976d-d759e74d017f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"6845-923d-ce78-44e9","ticket_type":"task","title":"Distinguish an unresolvable gate ref from a failed snapshot materialization in gate_ref_hash_basis","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e3091884-7d32-42b8-906e-291df5ae5157","116cfb5f-e5f8-4c81-a8cf-b835463599a4","b31800ca-c597-487a-ad39-1dad03c08a3d","f0ce8423-a442-4356-9f9e-6bb478272a5d","371f7749-e67d-46ee-9bd0-2a700197058d","92b4d716-6112-43cf-b1ca-7cc61ef63974","d863e47b-4672-47bd-890c-79305cab394a","170eab15-2431-4737-8171-6ee0d16919fa","92df7354-9687-4d15-a731-caf95e3a77b3","8dde1fe9-87d9-4792-bea7-44a1e905cebe","98ce43e1-172c-403f-976d-d759e74d017f","02a8ff29-4c02-4798-a074-c55925af5f86"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788804994891456760,"uuid":"05bafb90-4a14-46ac-929b-c73faf5a4383"}